.TH LALINFERENCE_MULTI_PIPE "1" "January 2026" "LALInference" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalinference_multi_pipe \- Setup a Condor DAG file to run the LALInference pipeline based on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lalinference_multi_pipe.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,config1.ini config2.ini \/\fR... \fI\,configN.ini\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Setup a Condor DAG file to run the LALInference pipeline based on
N config.ini files.
.PP
The user must specify either an injection file to analyse, with the \fB\-\-inj\fR option,
a list of SnglInspiralTable or CoincInspiralTable triggers with the \fB\-\-\fR<x>\-triggers options,
or an ASCII list of GPS times with the \fB\-\-gps\-time\-file\fR option.
.PP
The user must also specify and ini file which will contain the main analysis config.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-r\fR RUNDIR, \fB\-\-run\-path\fR=\fI\,RUNDIR\/\fR
Directory to run pipeline in (default: $PWD)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR LOGDIR, \fB\-\-daglog\-path\fR=\fI\,LOGDIR\/\fR
Path to directory to contain DAG log file. SHOULD BE
LOCAL TO SUBMIT NODE
.TP
\fB\-g\fR TIMES.txt, \fB\-\-gps\-time\-file\fR=\fI\,TIMES\/\fR.txt
Text file containing list of GPS times to analyse
.TP
\fB\-t\fR SNGL_FILE.xml, \fB\-\-single\-triggers\fR=\fI\,SNGL_FILE\/\fR.xml
SnglInspiralTable trigger list
.TP
\fB\-C\fR COINC_FILE.xml, \fB\-\-coinc\-triggers\fR=\fI\,COINC_FILE\/\fR.xml
CoinInspiralTable trigger list
.TP
\fB\-L\fR coinc_G0000.xml, \fB\-\-lvalert\fR=\fI\,coinc_G0000\/\fR.xml
LVAlert coinc file
.TP
\fB\-\-gid\fR=\fI\,GID\/\fR
Optional GraceDB ID for submitting results
.TP
\fB\-I\fR INJFILE.xml, \fB\-\-injections\fR=\fI\,INJFILE\/\fR.xml
List of injections to perform and analyse
.TP
\fB\-P\fR pipedown.sqlite, \fB\-\-pipedown\-db\fR=\fI\,pipedown\/\fR.sqlite
Pipedown database to read and analyse
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-folder\-names\fR
Space separated list of folders that will be created,
corresponding to the TIGER parameters that are being
tested or GR. The order has to be the same used with
the ini files!
.TP
\fB\-\-condor\-submit\fR
Automatically submit the condor dag
